  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>When <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>CH</mi></math> reacts with sodium an intermediate <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>≡</mo><mi>CNa</mi></math> is formed which on further reaction with propyl bromide gives <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>≡</mo><msub><mi>CCH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> as the product. The second step of the reaction follows, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></msub><mn>2</mn></math> mechanism.</p><p>The reaction is as follows,</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/eeb0ea7a-8cf1-486d-9f33-ce15143a5e9c.png\" style=\"width: 800px; height: 205px;\"/></p><p>Hence in the above reaction,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>≡</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><msup><mi>Na</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><mi>Br</mi></math></p><p>Hence option A is the answer.</p>",
    "image": null
